The vulnerable construct is present in the mbox_test_remove() function (lines 330-337). The function unconditionally frees both tx_channel and rx_channel without checking if they are aliased (pointing to the same underlying channel object). Specifically:

c
if (tdev->tx_channel)
    mbox_free_channel(tdev->tx_channel);
if (tdev->rx_channel)
    mbox_free_channel(tdev->rx_channel);


If tdev->tx_channel and tdev->rx_channel reference the same channel object (which is possible when a device tree configuration aliases both names to the same channel), this code will call mbox_free_channel() twice on the same channel, causing a double-free vulnerability. The fix would require checking if the two pointers are equal before freeing the second one, e.g., `if (tdev->rx_channel && tdev->rx_channel != tdev->tx_channel)`. This check is absent in the current code.
